# Your corporate address: the local seed makes it an organization admin, so you sign in as yourself.
# LOCAL_ADMIN_EMAIL=nome.sobrenome@uselets.com

# Local development needs no other environment: `bun run up` uses the containers in docker-compose.yml and
# the fixed ports in infra/local/config.ts. These exist to point a piece somewhere else on purpose.

# The dev database the local harness uses (refused unless it is the local container on :8200).
# DATABASE_URL=postgres://jiraia:jiraia@127.0.0.1:8200/jiraia

# Point `bun run web:dev` at a deployed API instead of local:serve, and stop sending x-local-user.
# VITE_API_URL=https://<api-id>.execute-api.us-east-1.amazonaws.com/dev
# VITE_LOCAL_AUTH=0

# In AWS the Lambdas get their configuration from template.yml (ADR-0025): DB_CLUSTER_ARN,
# DB_SECRET_ARN, DB_NAME, ALLOWED_EMAIL_DOMAINS, the Cognito pool (ADR-0026) and the rest.

# Locally there is no Cognito: `web:dev` signs in by e-mail through `x-local-user`. The domains the
# sign-in screen names can be set in apps/web/.env.local, which git ignores.
# VITE_ALLOWED_EMAIL_DOMAINS=uselets.com,lets.delivery
